// The /living/ hub has two jobs, and the order of the page reflects both.
//
//  1. It is the top-level local-services hub for people who already live here.
//     The service card grid therefore stays directly under the introduction,
//     above the long-form guide, rather than being pushed below several
//     thousand words of relocation copy.
//  2. It is the independent guide for people considering a move to Walton.
//
// Editorial source: Darren's approved, Harvard-referenced guide
// (walton-on-thames-living-guide-final-harvard.md, 15 September 2026). Every
// substantive claim below carries an inline author-date citation that links to
// its entry in the reference list at the foot of the page. Where a source was
// re-checked on 16 September 2026 and did not support the drafted wording, the
// wording was corrected rather than softened; those changes are recorded in
// docs/build-log.md.
//
// No FAQPage schema. Google restricts FAQ rich results to authoritative
// government and health sites, so the markup would describe visible content
// that will not be shown as a rich result. The questions are still real
// questions, marked up as ordinary headings and text, which is what both
// readers and answer engines actually need.
