        <h3 id="character">What living here is like</h3>
        <p>Walton combines three things that explain much of its modern appeal: <strong>London access, a functioning town centre and the River Thames</strong>.</p>
        <p>It is not one uniform suburban area. The historic streets around St Mary's and the river feel very different from the modern centre around The Heart. Ashley Park has a different housing character again, while the station and Halfway area are more convenient for rail commuters. Cottimore and Sidney Road preserve the layout of older estates, and north Walton has its own mixture of housing, sport and open space.</p>
        <p>That variation matters. A general description of Walton can only take a prospective resident so far, which is why the next section goes area by area.</p>

